<section class="copy-section copy-offer" id="assessment" aria-labelledby="assessment-heading"><div class="wrap copy-body"><div class="section-title"><h2 id="assessment-heading">The Assessment establishes your risks and the work</h2></div><div class="section-detail">
<p><strong>Private Exposure Assessment &#xB7; &#x20AA;3,600 including VAT &#xB7; Typically four hours</strong></p>
<p>Toza begins with your circumstances and the information you need to protect. We develop your personal threat model by examining relevant apps, devices, accounts, access arrangements and digital traces. The result is a specific risk assessment and priorities for hardening, identity/recovery changes and operational security practices.</p>
<p>The visit covers one main phone and one PC, iPad or second phone, with relevant identities, accounts, apps, permissions and recovery routes, including access to messages, photos, documents and location information. Review stays within what is disclosed, observable or otherwise lawfully accessible in your authorized environment and agreed scope.</p>
<p>You receive the risk assessment, priorities and ordered next steps in a practical summary of what was reviewed, found and changed and what remains. This establishes the plan for the full protection work. You receive the summary whether or not you continue.</p>
<p>If urgent exposure is identified, Toza will make the approved first-aid changes that can safely be completed within the visit&apos;s agreed scope. The Assessment completes the agreed intake, mapping, diagnosis and approved urgent first aid. Typically four hours is not an automatic cutoff or a trigger for another purchase.</p>
<p><a href="/en/private-exposure-assessment.html">The first paid visit in detail</a></p>
</div></div></section>
